# The guarded paths: the changes that always come back to Daniel for the per-head word, whatever
# the plan's scope. team-merge refuses a merge on Daniel's plan-time or standing word when a path
# the PR changes (each rename's old path too) matches a line, naming the path and the line's area.
# One pattern per line, its area first, then one space, then an extended regular expression
# (grep -E) matched case-insensitively against the whole repository path, and against it again
# with each camelCase hump split off by an underscore (LoginView.vue as Login_View.vue), so a
# word bounded by [^a-z0-9] matches inside such a name too; the permissions words take a digit as
# their right bound as well (OAuth2Callback.ts as O_Auth2_Callback.ts). The areas are exactly the
# ledger's guarded areas (guarded_areas in bin/lib/ledger.jq), kept in its order. The list errs
# wide: a change it guards needlessly only costs Daniel's per-head word, one it misses merges
# unseen.
